{"assumptions":[],"critic":[{"finding":"The brand wordmark \"Hive Works\" and the demo user's initials \"SC\" are hardcoded into the requirement, but they should come from configuration (sign-in and users are out of scope, so this identity is pure fixture data).","reqId":"REQ-10","rubric":8,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"The list operation accepts a status filter, but nothing says what happens when the filter value is missing, malformed or unsupported; no error path or AC covers it.","reqId":"REQ-5","rubric":2,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"Nothing covers the in-flight state while a status change is pending (e.g. disabling the action button), so a double-activation could send two transitions, such as Start work followed by an unintended second change.","reqId":"REQ-19","rubric":2,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"AC-4.1 only checks that each of the four operations \"returns a response\", so nothing observable confirms the \"exactly four and no others\" constraint beyond the edit/delete cases.","reqId":"REQ-4","rubric":3,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"AC-9.6 and AC-9.7 check that \"the request row retains its original status\", which is a database-level check rather than a public surface; unlike AC-9.4, they don't say to verify through a get-by-ID response.","reqId":"REQ-9","rubric":3,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"Only the Title error message text is specified; the UI messages for missing area and missing priority are undefined, even though REQ-14 requires a field error under each failing field.","reqId":"REQ-14","rubric":2,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"Cancel behaviour in the create dialog (whether entered values are discarded and the dialog closes without a request) has no requirement or AC.","reqId":"REQ-12","rubric":2,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"Creation times are stored in UTC (REQ-6) but displayed as a date with no timezone, and the spec never says which timezone decides the calendar date, so the list and detail screens could disagree with test expectations near midnight.","reqId":"REQ-23","rubric":1,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"AC-21.1 depends on subjective judgments (\"readable text\", \"neutral\", \"near-black\") and gives no concrete colour values, so there is no objective pass/fail check for the \"specified badge colors\".","reqId":"REQ-21","rubric":3,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"AC-16.1's loading state is a manual check of a transient condition, and the spec defines no way to hold or simulate the pending list request so it can be observed reliably.","reqId":"REQ-16","rubric":3,"severity":"low"}],"lint":[{"check":"L1 ids","details":"ok","passed":true},{"check":"L2 req-ac","details":"ok","passed":true},{"check":"L3 ears","details":"ok","passed":true},{"check":"L4 vague","details":"ok","passed":true},{"check":"L5 nfr","details":"ok","passed":true},{"check":"L6 scope","details":"ok","passed":true},{"check":"L8 anchors","details":"ok","passed":true},{"check":"L10 trace","details":"ok","passed":true},{"check":"L11 observable","details":"ok","passed":true},{"check":"L12 literals","details":"REQ-22 hardcodes \"1280\"; should it be configuration?; REQ-23 hardcodes \"2026\"; should it be configuration?","passed":false}],"nfrs":[{"id":"NFR-1","metric":"At viewport widths of 375 px and 1280 px, there is no horizontal page scroll; the list uses cards at 375 px and table rows at 1280 px.","text":"The Requests list shall adapt its layout for narrow and wide viewports without horizontal page scrolling."},{"id":"NFR-2","metric":"Contrast ratio is at least 4.5:1 for normal text and 3:1 for large text.","text":"Text shall meet WCAG AA contrast requirements."}],"outOfScope":["Dedicated support guarantees for named browsers (Q-2).","Sign-in, roles, additional users, search, sorting choices, pagination, comments, attachments, assignees, due dates, notifications, email, live updates, dark mode, and animation.","Configurable table-layout viewport target (Q-6).","Additional request-detail fetch states for loading or failures other than an unknown ID (Q-7)."],"requirements":[{"acceptance":[{"given":"The application is running and a client has valid request fields.","id":"AC-1.1","level":"api","then":"The create response record and get-by-ID response record contain the same ID and values for every request field.","when":"The client creates a request through the HTTP API, records the create response, and retrieves the returned ID through a separate get-by-ID API call."},{"given":"The application is running.","id":"AC-1.2","level":"manual","then":"The Requests screen is displayed.","when":"A user opens the application in a browser."}],"ears":"The maintenance request system shall provide a browser-accessible web front end, an HTTP API, and a database that stores request records.","id":"REQ-1","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","Q-8"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The database is empty before first initialization.","id":"AC-2.1","level":"api","then":"The response list has a count of 8, with status counts of 4 Open, 2 In progress, and 2 Done; exactly one Open request has Urgent priority, and the list includes every supported area.","when":"The application initializes and a client lists all requests through the API."}],"ears":"When an empty database is initialized, the maintenance request system shall seed exactly eight requests: four Open including exactly one Urgent, two In progress, and two Done, with every supported area represented.","id":"REQ-2","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-2"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A request has been created and its ID recorded.","id":"AC-3.1","level":"api","then":"The response record contains the created request's ID and field values.","when":"The application service is restarted and a client retrieves that ID through the API."},{"given":"A request is visible in the Requests list.","id":"AC-3.2","level":"manual","then":"The screen shows the persisted request row.","when":"The browser page is reloaded."}],"ears":"The maintenance request system shall persist request records across browser reloads and application restarts.","id":"REQ-3","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-3"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The API is available.","id":"AC-4.1","level":"api","then":"Each call returns a response for its corresponding request operation.","when":"A client invokes list, create, get by ID, and change status using HTTP calls."},{"given":"A request exists and its current record has been retrieved.","id":"AC-4.2","level":"api","then":"Each call returns an error response and the request record remains unchanged.","when":"A client attempts to edit a fixed request field or delete the request through the API."}],"ears":"The API shall expose exactly four request operations and no others: list requests, create a request, get a request by ID, and change a request's status.","id":"REQ-4","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-4"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Requests with different statuses and creation times exist.","id":"AC-5.1","level":"api","then":"The first response list contains all requests newest first, and the filtered response list contains only matching statuses newest first.","when":"A client lists requests without a status and then lists requests with one status filter."}],"ears":"When a client lists requests, the API shall return all requests or only requests matching one requested status, ordered newest first.","id":"REQ-5","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-4"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A client has valid request fields.","id":"AC-6.1","level":"api","then":"The response record contains a system-generated ID, a UTC creation time, and status Open.","when":"The client creates a request through the API."}],"ears":"When a client creates a valid request, the maintenance request system shall assign an ID and UTC creation time and set its status to Open.","id":"REQ-6","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-4"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A client submits requests with a missing title, a two-character title, a title over 80 characters, a missing or unsupported area, a missing or unsupported priority, or a description over 500 characters.","id":"AC-7.1","level":"api","then":"Each invalid response contains an error naming the invalid field, and the two-character title response contains “Title must be 3 to 80 characters.”","when":"The client sends each request to the create API operation."},{"given":"A client submits a title with surrounding whitespace that leaves 3 to 80 characters after trimming, and a title containing only whitespace in a separate request.","id":"AC-7.2","level":"api","then":"The valid response record contains the trimmed title, and the invalid response contains a Title error.","when":"The client creates both requests through the API."}],"ears":"When a client submits a request for creation, the maintenance request system shall require a title trimmed to 3 to 80 characters, an area of Kitchen, Meeting room, Open desk, Washroom, or Reception, a priority of Low, Normal, or Urgent, and an optional description of at most 500 characters, rejecting invalid values with an error naming the field.","id":"REQ-7","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-4","Q-4"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A request exists with known title, area, priority, and description values.","id":"AC-8.1","level":"api","then":"The response is an error and the retrieved record retains its original field values.","when":"A client attempts to change each of those fields or delete the request through the API."}],"ears":"The API shall keep title, area, priority, and description fixed after creation and reject attempts to change those fields or delete a request.","id":"REQ-8","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-4"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A request has status Open.","id":"AC-9.1","level":"api","then":"The response record has status In progress.","when":"A client changes its status to In progress through the API."},{"given":"A request has status In progress.","id":"AC-9.2","level":"api","then":"The response record has status Done.","when":"A client changes its status to Done through the API."},{"given":"A request has status Done.","id":"AC-9.3","level":"api","then":"The response record has status Open.","when":"A client changes its status to Open through the API."},{"given":"A request has status Open.","id":"AC-9.4","level":"api","then":"The response is an error and the retrieved record still has status Open.","when":"A client attempts to change its status directly to Done."},{"given":"No request has the ID supplied to the status-change operation.","id":"AC-9.5","level":"api","then":"The response identifies the request as not found.","when":"A client attempts to change status for that ID through the API."},{"given":"A request exists and its current record has been retrieved.","id":"AC-9.6","level":"api","then":"The response is an error and the request row retains its original status.","when":"A client sends a status-change request with no body."},{"given":"A request exists and its current record has been retrieved.","id":"AC-9.7","level":"api","then":"The response is an error and the request row retains its original status.","when":"A client sends a status-change request with an unrecognized status value."}],"ears":"The maintenance request API shall accept only Open to In progress, In progress to Done, and Done to Open status transitions, reject all other status changes, return a not-found response for a status change on an unknown request ID, and return an error without changing any request when the status-change body is missing or its status value is unrecognized.","id":"REQ-9","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-4"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The Requests screen has loaded.","id":"AC-10.1","level":"manual","then":"The screen displays the Hive Works wordmark, SC, the four filter choices with All selected, the New request button, and the request list.","when":"A user views the screen before changing any filter."}],"ears":"The Requests screen shall display the Hive Works wordmark, the signed-in demo user's initials SC, a status filter with All, Open, In progress, and Done choices with All selected initially, a New request button, and a newest-first request list.","id":"REQ-10","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-5"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The Requests screen is showing a selected status filter.","id":"AC-11.1","level":"manual","then":"The screen retains the selected filter and displays a refreshed list in which a request that no longer matches may be absent.","when":"The user opens a request detail screen, changes its status successfully, and returns to the Requests screen."},{"given":"The Requests screen is loaded.","id":"AC-11.2","level":"manual","then":"The screen displays the refreshed list for that filter.","when":"The user selects a status filter."}],"ears":"When a user selects a status filter or returns from request detail, the Requests screen shall load the list for the selected filter and retain that filter on return from detail.","id":"REQ-11","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-5","Q-5"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The Requests screen is displayed.","id":"AC-12.1","level":"manual","then":"The screen shows a dialog with labeled Title, Area, Priority, and Description fields, Normal selected for Priority, and Create and Cancel controls.","when":"The user activates New request."}],"ears":"When the user opens New request, the Requests screen shall show a dialog with Title, Area, Priority defaulting to Normal, and Description fields, plus Create and Cancel controls.","id":"REQ-12","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-5"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The create dialog is open and a filter other than All is selected.","id":"AC-13.1","level":"manual","then":"The screen closes the dialog, selects All, and shows the new Open request row at the top of the list.","when":"The user submits valid request fields and the create API call succeeds."}],"ears":"When valid request creation succeeds, the Requests screen shall close the dialog, select All, and show the new Open request at the top of the list.","id":"REQ-13","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-5","Q-1"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The create dialog is open.","id":"AC-14.1","level":"manual","then":"The screen keeps the dialog open and displays “Title must be 3 to 80 characters.” under the Title field.","when":"The user submits a title of two characters."}],"ears":"When a create field fails validation, the Requests screen shall keep the dialog open and display the field's error message under that field.","id":"REQ-14","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-5"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The create dialog contains entered values.","id":"AC-15.1","level":"manual","then":"The screen displays “Could not create request.” in the dialog, retains the entered field values, and shows an enabled retry path through Create.","when":"The create API call fails for a non-validation reason."}],"ears":"When the create API call fails for a reason other than field validation, the Requests screen shall show “Could not create request.” in the dialog, retain entered values, and allow retry.","id":"REQ-15","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-5","Q-3"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The Requests list request is in progress.","id":"AC-16.1","level":"manual","then":"The screen displays “Loading requests…”.","when":"The user views the Requests screen."},{"given":"No requests match the selected filter.","id":"AC-16.2","level":"manual","then":"The screen displays “No requests here.”","when":"The Requests screen finishes loading the list."},{"given":"The list API call fails.","id":"AC-16.3","level":"manual","then":"The screen displays “Could not load requests.” and a Retry button.","when":"The Requests screen handles the failure."}],"ears":"While requests are loading, absent for the selected filter, or fail to load, the Requests screen shall display the corresponding loading, empty, or error state with retry available for load errors.","id":"REQ-16","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-5"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A request with a description and a request without a description both exist.","id":"AC-17.1","level":"manual","then":"Each screen displays the request fields, badges, created date, and back link, and the screen for the request without a description displays “No description.”","when":"The user opens each request detail screen."}],"ears":"When a request exists, the request detail screen shall display a back link, its title, area, priority badge, status badge, created date, and description or “No description.” when the description is empty.","id":"REQ-17","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-6","Q-7"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Requests exist in Open, In progress, and Done statuses.","id":"AC-18.1","level":"manual","then":"The screen shows Start work, Mark done, and Reopen for the corresponding statuses.","when":"The user opens each request detail screen."}],"ears":"The request detail screen shall show Start work for Open, Mark done for In progress, and Reopen for Done.","id":"REQ-18","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-6"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A request detail screen shows its current status and action button.","id":"AC-19.1","level":"manual","then":"After the response, the screen displays the new status badge and the corresponding next action button.","when":"The user activates the button and the status API call succeeds."},{"given":"A request detail screen shows its current status and action button.","id":"AC-19.2","level":"manual","then":"The screen displays “Could not update the request.” and retains the prior status badge.","when":"The user activates the button and the status API call fails."}],"ears":"When a status change succeeds or fails, the request detail screen shall show the new status and corresponding action only after success, or show “Could not update the request.” while retaining the prior status after failure.","id":"REQ-19","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-6"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"No request has the ID in the address.","id":"AC-20.1","level":"manual","then":"The screen displays “Request not found.” and a link back to the Requests screen.","when":"The user opens the detail screen for that ID."},{"given":"No request has the requested ID.","id":"AC-20.2","level":"api","then":"The response identifies the request as not found.","when":"A client gets that ID through the API."}],"ears":"When a request ID does not exist, the request detail screen shall display “Request not found.” and a link back to the Requests screen.","id":"REQ-20","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-6","Q-7"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The Requests and request detail screens are displayed.","id":"AC-21.1","level":"manual","then":"The screens show a light theme, sans-serif text, neutral background, near-black text, Open blue, In progress amber, Done green, Urgent red, Low and Normal neutral, and readable text on every badge.","when":"A person inspects the theme and badges."}],"ears":"The maintenance request screens shall use one light theme, one sans-serif font, a neutral background, near-black text, and the specified status and priority badge colors with text labels on every badge.","id":"REQ-21","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-7"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The Requests and detail screens are available.","id":"AC-22.1","level":"manual","then":"The screen dates contain no time, the Requests list uses cards at 375 px and table rows at 1280 px, neither screen has horizontal page scroll, every field has a label, every control is keyboard reachable, and text meets WCAG AA contrast.","when":"A person inspects created dates and tests the screens at 375 px and 1280 px, including keyboard navigation and contrast."}],"ears":"The maintenance request screens shall show request dates as date-only values, use stacked cards at 375 px and table rows at the fixed 1280 px viewport target, avoid horizontal page scrolling at those widths, label every field, and make every control keyboard reachable with WCAG AA text contrast.","id":"REQ-22","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-5","I-6","I-7","Q-6"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A request has a stored UTC creation time.","id":"AC-23.1","level":"manual","then":"The screen shows a date-only value such as “8 Oct 2026” with no time or timezone.","when":"The Requests list or detail screen displays that request."}],"ears":"The maintenance request system shall display created dates as date-only values such as “8 Oct 2026” without a time or timezone.","id":"REQ-23","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-5","I-6"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The automated business-rule test suite is available.","id":"AC-24.1","level":"job","then":"The test run status is passed and its result list includes valid creation with Open status, missing and too-short title rejection, missing area rejection, too-long description rejection, all three allowed transitions, rejection of a disallowed transition, filtered newest-first listing, and unknown-ID not-found behavior.","when":"The test job runs."},{"given":"The end-to-end test suite is available.","id":"AC-24.2","level":"job","then":"The test run status is passed and its result list shows the created request at the top, then in the Done-filtered list after completion.","when":"The end-to-end test job runs the list, create, open, Start work, Mark done, and Done-filter workflow."}],"ears":"The maintenance request application shall include automated tests for the request business rules and an end-to-end list-to-completion workflow.","id":"REQ-24","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-8"]}],"roundTrip":{"droppedSpans":[],"inventedCapabilities":[]},"settled":[{"decision":"Should the 1280 px table-layout target be configurable, or remain the fixed target specified for this release? → Keep 1280 px as the fixed table-layout target.","how":"answered","kind":"lint","problem":"L12 literals: REQ-22 hardcodes \"1280\"; should it be configuration?; REQ-23 hardcodes \"2026\"; should it be configuration?","ref":"Q-6"},{"decision":"Should the request detail screen add states for loading a request and for failures other than not-found? → Keep the specified detail behavior: show the request on success and “Request not found.” for an unknown ID; add no other fetch states.","how":"answered","kind":"critic","problem":"The detail screen has no loading state and no load-failure state for errors other than not-found (such as a network or server error); only success and \"Request not found.\" are covered.","ref":"Q-7"},{"decision":"How should AC-1.1 verify that a newly created request can be retrieved? → Compare the create response with a separate get-by-ID API response.","how":"answered","kind":"critic","problem":"AC-1.1 passes or fails on \"the database row\", which is internal storage rather than a public surface; it needs to compare the create response against a separate API get-by-ID response.","ref":"Q-8"}]}